0 Differential
0 Name: differential.ldr
0 Author: erik-larsen
0 // A differential on a stand. An 8 tooth gear on the input axle drives the housing's 24 tooth
0 // ring. Inside, a bevel gear on each output axle meshes with a third (planet) bevel gear on a
0 // post in the housing. With nothing on the ground the stand is held still, and the two outputs
0 // can turn at different speeds: turning the input turns both the same way, and holding the
0 // input still lets one output turn the other the opposite way.

0 // Step 1: a 6x8 plate with two 1x6 bricks and two Technic 1x6 bricks on top
1 71 0 0 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3036.dat
1 14 0 -24 60 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 0 -24 -60 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 0 -48 60 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
1 14 0 -48 -60 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 2: the differential housing, centred between the bricks at hole height
1 71 0 -38 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 6573.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 3: output axles with a bevel gear each, teeth facing the middle (17 LDU out)
1 0 0 -38 -55 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 32073.dat
1 71 0 -38 -17 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 6589.dat
1 0 0 -38 55 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 32073.dat
1 71 0 -38 17 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 6589.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 4: the planet bevel gear on the housing's post, teeth facing up into the middle
1 71 0 -21 0 1 0 0 0 0 -1 0 1 0 6589.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 5: input axle with an 8 tooth gear meshing the 24 tooth ring (turned half a tooth)
1 0 40 -38 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3707.dat
1 72 40 -38 30 0.92388 -0.382683 0 0.382683 0.92388 0 0 0 1 3647.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 6: a wheel rim on each output
1 71 0 -38 90 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3482.dat
1 71 0 -38 -90 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 3482.dat
0 STEP
